the latest release is den v2.0.0, a new major version, and `den update` does not cross one: v2 is a rewrite that does not read v1's config (~/.den/config.yaml, stacks, nests) and cannot list or remove v1 sandboxes. Before switching, commit and push your work, then run `den rm <sandbox>` on each v1 sandbox with this binary (den v1.13.1) — once it is replaced, nothing is left that can remove them or the git worktrees they registered. The steps are in https://github.com/PillowPillow/den/blob/main/docs/migrating-from-v1.md; then install v2 with `curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PillowPillow/den/main/install.sh | sh` (or `brew upgrade --cask den`)